  "faithful": "The conferve of mint retains the taste and virtues of the herb. It is given in weaknesses of the stomach and retchings to vomit; and not unfrequently does service in some cases of this kind, where the warmer and more active preparations of mint would be less proper.",
  "modern": "The conserve of mint retains the taste and virtues of the herb. It is given in weaknesses of the stomach and retchings to vomit; and not unfrequently does service in some cases of this kind, where the warmer and more active preparations of mint would be less proper."
